            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "## About the data\r\n\r\n| Data | Source |\r\n| --- | --- |\r\n| VM and VMSS size, region, zone and capacity | `microsoft.compute/virtualmachines`, `microsoft.compute/virtualmachinescalesets` |\r\n| Autoscale minimum and maximum | `microsoft.insights/autoscalesettings` |\r\n| Retirement metadata and impact | `providers/Microsoft.Advisor/metadata`, `advisorresources` |\r\n| Advisories | `ServiceHealthResources` |\r\n| Feb 2027 price change | VM size and region, from Microsoft's announced lists |\r\n\r\n* Capacity limitation isn't a shutdown notice: VMs keep running until their retirement date. The v4 restrictions were lifted.\r\n* Price rules: v1/v2 +25% in every region. Other series: North Europe +17%, France Central/South +11%, West Europe and Norway East/West +9%, Southeast Asia +8%. Dsv7, Ddsv7, Dlsv7, Dldsv7, Esv7 and Edsv7 are excluded; sovereign clouds are exempt.\r\n* Reservations, savings plans and negotiated prices aren't read. Storage price changes aren't covered.\r\n* **VM SKU retirements** can also include image, extension and platform-feature retirements.\r\n* The workbook can't guarantee quota or capacity. Target families are directional.\r\n* Compute without a VM or VMSS resource, such as Azure Batch pools, isn't covered.\r\n\r\n**Affected series:** F, Fs, Fsv2; D, Ds, Dv2, Dsv2, Dv3, Dsv3; B, Bs, Av2, Amv2; Ev3, Esv3; G, Gs; Ls, Lsv2."
            },
